# CTF10 public storage to surface binding: source proposal

This package proposes one standalone public module and seven focused contractual
tests. It adds only a module declaration to the existing heat-balance parent.
No cache, initializer, surface solver, weather, history or reporting path calls it.
Sources and tests have not been imported, compiled, formatted or executed.

## Actual owner handoff

`capture_public_ctf_surface_generation(model, initialization, context)` borrows
the actual `TypedModel` and actual `OrderedCtfPublicInitialization`. The caller
must supply the producer's real caller inputs, incoming shared flags/aggregates,
and producer revision identity from the same generation. Capture never invents
that identity or derives a timestep from coefficients. It is a transport API,
not retroactive authentication of independently supplied objects. A future
ordinary producer integration must own this handoff immediately after generation.

`CtfPublicSurfaceGeneration::bind_surface(SurfaceId)` follows the actual surface's
`ConstructionId` to the actual declared public row. IDs need not be dense and
surface order need not match construction order. It checks row index, original
material IDs and actual used-construction membership at capture. Reverse storage
retains the already selected provider; binding checks its earlier declaration,
ID/use/returned owner and reversed original stack. It never reselects a provider
from numerical layers or computes/copies reverse coefficients.

The binding borrows all twelve public arrays, all nineteen slots of each, actual
NumCTFTerms, NumHistories, CTFTimeStep and UValue without arithmetic. Reset,
severe, unavailable, selected fatal/scope/capacity stop, incomplete prefix,
shared ErrorsFound, duplicate IDs and unsupported families/boundaries are typed
unavailable. These are adapter scope/representability decisions, not new Native
guards or reconstructed process outcomes. Whole-Init reports/final fatal/backend
completion remain unproved even when this selected binding returns.

## Exact generation key

The key uses structured exact equality, not an aggregate R/C digest. Its private
fields retain actual producer revision, compiled timestep count and supplied
caller timestep bits; incoming ErrorsFound/DoCTFErrorReport, SimpleCTFOnly and
MaxCTFTerms; actual EMS/override flags; every material in original registry order
with ID/name/family, roughness, thickness/k/rho/cp/stored resistance and all three
absorptance bits; every declared construction in original order with ID/name,
raw outside layer, raw layers and effective original stack; every surface's
ordered ID/construction/boundary binding; every public row's ID/index/original
stack/use/invocation/entry-return flags/route or typed error; all twelve arrays'
bits/counts/timestep/U; and actual selected aggregate/stop/completion owners.

Only plain ordinary opaque no-source Construction plus Regular/NoMass materials
and Outdoors/Adiabatic bindings are admitted. Unsupported construction options
and material families fail explicitly; no unsupported payload is silently omitted
from a successful key. EIO rows and old legacy R/C fallback do not generate this
selected public owner and are not substituted. Roughness/absorptance and raw
registry/order details are conservative extra invalidation dependencies.

The key is for selected coefficient generation and identity binding. It is NOT
a weather/environment/geometry/history key. Geometry/weather changes still need
their own real environment transition and history reinitialization contract.
This proposal creates no history values, so it cannot authorize reusing old
histories after those inputs change. A future mutable cache must compare the full
key and rebind/reinitialize at the real lifecycle boundary; current cache hash
and self-comparison token behavior are not changed here.

## Uninitialized history contract

The returned contract retains all four Native fixed19 history capacities, active
coefficient slots0..NumCTFTerms, actual construction history count and timestep,
actual zone timestep/U, and GLOBAL selected Init aggregate. It states the exact
Native allocation predicate `!SimpleCTFOnly || AnyEnergyManagementSystemInModel`
and update predicate `SimpleCTFOnly && !AnyConstrOverridesInModel` as requirements,
without allocating values or executing either branch. Dynamic controls are outside
this selected CON-01 adapter. A required public/global count outside0..18 or
nonpositive NumHistories is an unsupported history contract, not a Native clamp.

Native history arrays use term1 for current and term2 for first past value;
coefficient current index0 is distinct. Later initialization must preserve real
SurfInitialTemp=23.0 separately from the user zone-air seed (currently20 in the
candidate observer), and source per-surface environment owners. In particular,
inside flux term1 reads the then-existing outside flux term2 before the source
term2 assignment; a uniform fill is not equivalent. Simple shifting uses GLOBAL
MaxCTFTerms+1, not local Vec length. Master/counter/SumTime and literal interpolation
remain entirely pending. Raw separately owns genuine normal Native lifecycle
observation preparation; no results from it are operands here.

## Source validation and limits

The seven unexecuted tests use actual typed all-resistive preprocessing/initial/
first-assembly/retry/public APIs for the basic owner fixture. Explicit later
mutations exercise only binding/key contracts: non-dense identities, all12 tails,
signed zero/NaN payload preservation, stored Regular resistance and ordered input
changes, caller/revision inputs, reverse-provider custody, separate dt/history/
global master requirements, and required missing/error/severe/capacity/unsupported
cases. They do not supply expected Native coefficients or certify massive output.

Prospective copy validation is exact class/shape/bits (all12x19 and metadata);
there is no arithmetic tolerance or new science gate in this adapter. Future
consumer arithmetic, environment initialization, history advancement, weather,
inside/outside balance and reporting must have their own pre-output scope and
genuine same-input Native observations. No CTF10 full gate or surface handoff
PASS is claimed. Plan/card and all earlier immutable holds remain unchanged.

Header authored the prior public/storage and assembly/ingress sources. This new
proposal requires Root and another author's full source review; self-read is
source/API preparation, not independent formula certification.
